Vendored third-party code keeps its own licence, which travels beside it:

  Lua 5.4, by Lua.org / PUC-Rio, MIT
      lua/upstream/, and the notice is at the bottom of lua.h

  stb_truetype.h, stb_image.h and stb_image_write.h, by Sean Barrett, MIT or public domain
      runtime/upstream/stb/, notice at the bottom of each header,
      pointed at by LICENSE.stb beside them, which also records the
      version and commit each was taken from

  puff.c, by Mark Adler, zlib licence
      runtime/upstream/puff/LICENSE.puff

  miniz 3.0.2, by Rich Geldreich, RAD Game Tools and Valve Software, MIT
      runtime/upstream/miniz/LICENSE; its deflater makes the zips Tracker
      compresses, and README.md beside it says how it is built

  musl's maths functions, by Rich Felker and others, MIT
      runtime/upstream/musl-math/COPYRIGHT, which also lists the other
      permissive notices parts of musl carry; the vendoring is recorded
      in README.kosmos.md beside it

  TinyGL, by Fabrice Bellard and erysdren, MIT
      runtime/upstream/tinygl/COPYING, with the vendoring recorded in
      README.kosmos.md beside it

  NetSurf's libraries, by J-M Bell and the NetSurf Browser Project, MIT
      runtime/upstream/netsurf/: libcss, libdom, libhubbub, libparserutils
      and libwapcaplet, each under the COPYING file in its own directory

  minimp3, by lieff, CC0 1.0 (public domain)
      runtime/upstream/minimp3/LICENSE, and the notice at the top of
      minimp3.h

  minih264, by lieff, CC0 1.0 (public domain)
      runtime/upstream/minih264/LICENSE, and the notice at the top of
      minih264e.h

  minimp4, by lieff, CC0 1.0 (public domain)
      runtime/upstream/minimp4/LICENSE, and the notice at the top of
      minimp4.h

  ufbx, by Samuli Raivio, MIT or public domain
      runtime/upstream/ufbx/LICENSE, with the vendoring recorded in
      README.kosmos.md beside it

  luacheck, by Peter Melnichenko and contributors, MIT
      runtime/upstream/luacheck/LICENSE, with the vendoring recorded in
      README.kosmos.md beside it; and the SHA-1 it carries, under
      src/luacheck/vendor/sha1/LICENSE

  LakeSnes, by angelo_wf and contributors, the CX4 by dink, MIT
      runtime/upstream/lakesnes/LICENSE.txt, with the vendoring recorded
      in README.kosmos.md beside it. Built by default, in `FULL=1`

  The fonts
      assets/fonts/, each under the LICENSE file beside it. A font
      whose licence is not beside it is not committed, and the build
      says so when it finds one.

  Lucide's icons, by Lucide Icons and Contributors, ISC
      assets/icons/lucide/, under the LICENSE beside them, which also
      gives the MIT terms of the icons derived from Feather, by Cole
      Bemis; the vendoring is recorded in README.kosmos.md, and the line
      icons rendered from them into assets/icons/line/ carry the same terms

  The Haiku icons, by Haiku, Inc., MIT
      assets/icons/, under the LICENSE beside them. The Haiku logo and
      leaf are Haiku, Inc.'s trademarks, and neither is among them

  The wallpapers, photographs from Unsplash, under the Unsplash License
      assets/wallpapers/, under the LICENSE beside them, each credited to
      its photographer in the README there. Scaled to 1920x1080 by
      tools/wallpapers.sh. In `FULL=1` images only

None of those are modified in place. Changes to them are build steps, so
what is in this tree is what their authors released.

Three more are copyleft: two under the GPL, and FFmpeg's decoder under the
LGPL. Nothing here is linked dynamically - whatever is compiled into an
image is linked into it - so an image carrying either GPL one is a combined
work under the GPL as a whole. Kosmos's own sources stay MIT either way.

  FFmpeg's H.264 decoder, by the FFmpeg developers, LGPL 2.1 or later
      runtime/upstream/ffmpeg/, in COPYING.LGPLv2.1 and LICENSE.md, with
      the vendoring recorded in README.kosmos.md beside it: the 95 files
      the H.264 Kit's entry points reach, unmodified. Built by default
      (`FULL=1`) and left out of `make FULL=0`, `make test` and
      `make bench`. Every source in this tree is public, so the image can
      be relinked against a changed FFmpeg, which is what the LGPL asks
      of a static link.

  doomgeneric, id Software's Doom by way of Chocolate Doom, GPLv2
      runtime/upstream/doom/, in LICENSE.doomgeneric. Not in the system's
      image in any build: `make apps` links it into doom.elf, Doom's own
      image, installed in /Home/Apps/Doom beside doom.lua, and that image
      is the GPLv2 work.

  Chocolate Quake, by id Software, Henrique Barateli and others, GPL
      runtime/upstream/quake/, with the vendoring recorded in
      README.kosmos.md beside it. Every source file carries id's
      "version 2, or any later version" notice, and the project's own
      LICENSE file is version 3. Not built by default: Quake is included
      only under `make QUAKE=1` and `make MEGA=1`, and `FULL=1` does not
      turn it on.
